    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0593" n="509" xml:id="pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/368</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-21T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 21, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5459. Department informed that Thomas Cook &amp; Son, London, are authorized by
                    British Government under certain conditions to forward limited sums of money to
                    British or Allied nationals in Russian Poland under German occupation. Please
                    ascertain and report exact channels used for forwarding of these remittances,
                    especially whether payments have to be made through a bank in Germany as the
                    Department understands is the case. How are payments effected in Poland and how
                    are receipts from payees obtained and returned to London?</p>
                <p>Have you yet forwarded to Department the memorandum mentioned in the last
                    sentence of your despatch No. 6503 of June 29 last?<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d608-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
